flowchart TD
A["Order saved: gather account, contact, items, pricing, warehouse, shipping and tax info"] --> B{"Has open cases on account?"}
B -->|Any outcome| C{"Is order activated?"}
C --> D{"Rush, standard or unknown order type"}
D --> E{"Which account tier"}
E --> F{"On credit hold?"}
F --> G{"Enough stock in warehouse?"}
G --> H{"Domestic or international shipping?"}
H --> I{"Volume or loyalty discount applies?"}
I --> J{"Order taxable?"}
J --> K{"Delivery overdue past 7 days?"}
K --> L{"Express or ground carrier?"}
L --> M{"Notify contact or owner only?"}
M --> N["Reserve stock for each line item"]
N --> O["Send confirmation email and post to account feed"]
O --> P["Notify warehouse, finance and account owner"]
P --> Q["Schedule delivery, log fulfilment and mark order fulfilled"]
```

This diagram traces the order's journey from initial data gathering through a long sequence of status checks (activation, type, tier, credit hold, stock, region, discount, tax, open cases, delivery timing, carrier, and notification preference), each of which stamps a fulfilment stage on the order. It then loops through line items to reserve stock, sends confirmation notifications to the customer and internal teams, and finishes by scheduling delivery and closing out the order as fulfilled.
